<BaseLayout title="Nominations"><article class="standard-page"><header class="page-heading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Awards &amp; recognition</p><h1>Nominations</h1><p class="standfirst">How TSQ selects and announces nominations for published work.</p></header><div class="gh-content"><p>TSQ wants strong work to travel beyond the magazine. Where a piece is eligible, our editors may nominate published work for external prizes, anthologies and annual best-of collections.</p><h2>How nominations work</h2><p>Nominations are selected by the editors from work published by TSQ. Writers and artists do not need to pay a fee or submit their work to us again for consideration.</p><p>Eligibility, category limits and deadlines vary by award. When TSQ makes nominations, we will announce them on this page and through our usual channels.</p><h2>Awards we may consider</h2><p>Depending on eligibility and the work we publish, this may include the Pushcart Prize, Best of the Net, Best Small Fictions and other category-specific opportunities. Visual work may also be considered for Best of the Net’s Art category and other appropriate visual-art or photography awards and annuals where publication or editor entry is permitted.</p><p>Being published by TSQ does not guarantee a nomination, and nomination decisions remain editorial.</p><h2>Current nominations</h2><p>No nominations have been announced yet.</p></div></article></BaseLayout>
